1
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:00,559
Hi, Mom.

2
00:01:00,559 --> 00:01:11,894
Hi, Robbie.

3
00:01:11,894 --> 00:01:14,008
You're home from school early.

4
00:01:14,008 --> 00:01:17,856
Yeah, they're getting the assembly hall

5
00:01:17,856 --> 00:01:23,383
ready for the graduation ceremony,

6
00:01:23,383 --> 00:02:23,612
so we all got to go home early.

7
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:26,670
Too noisy to study.

8
00:02:26,670 --> 00:02:27,773
Well, now that you're here,

9
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:29,312
you can help me with dinner.

10
00:02:29,312 --> 00:02:32,621
I need those potatoes peeled and sliced.

11
00:02:32,621 --> 00:02:35,485
Mom, give me a break.

12
00:02:35,485 --> 00:02:40,810
Alexandra's coming over to help me study for my math final Alexandra

13
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:41,850
Well, in that case,

14
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:46,766
you can wash the dishes and clean up after dinner.

15
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:49,026
Can I invite Alexandra to stay for dinner?

16
00:02:49,026 --> 00:02:49,744
Of course.

17
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:52,722
Thanks, Mom.

18
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:55,700
You and Alexandra

19
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,894
have become good friends, haven't you?

20
00:02:57,894 --> 00:02:59,398
Yes. I like her.

21
00:02:59,398 --> 00:03:00,488
She's a terrific person.

22
00:03:00,488 --> 00:03:05,099
I'm going to miss her

23
00:03:05,099 --> 00:03:06,496
when she goes back to Greece.

24
00:03:06,496 --> 00:03:10,237
Would you like to give her a little farewell party?

25
00:03:10,237 --> 00:03:14,067
Mom, that would be terrific!

26
00:03:14,067 --> 00:03:17,167
Maybe we could make it a surprise.

27
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:18,201
Oh, I don't know.

28
00:03:18,201 --> 00:03:20,856
Surprise parties don't always work out.

29
00:03:20,856 --> 00:03:23,626
Well, we could tell her

30
00:03:23,626 --> 00:03:26,039
it's a graduation party for me.

31
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,719
When Alexandra arrives,

32
00:03:27,719 --> 00:03:29,790
we'll surprise her.

33
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:33,715
Well, I suppose that might work.

34
00:03:33,715 --> 00:03:38,157
I'd like to give her a nice going-away present.

35
00:03:38,157 --> 00:03:38,357
Fine.

36
00:03:38,157 --> 00:03:40,369
There's only one problem.

37
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:43,347
What's that?

38
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:44,077
I'm broke.

39
00:03:44,077 --> 00:03:46,325
I should have saved some money.

40
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:47,450
I'm sure Alexandra

41
00:03:47,450 --> 00:03:50,647
would be happy with something simple, Robbie.

42
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:52,281
I know.

43
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:52,877
But, well,

44
00:03:52,877 --> 00:03:54,963
I'd like to give her something nice

45
00:03:54,963 --> 00:03:58,211
to remember me by.

46
00:03:58,211 --> 00:04:01,446
Maybe I could borrow some money from you and Dad.

47
00:04:01,446 --> 00:04:02,600
It's all right with me

48
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,193
if it's all right with your dad.

49
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:04,993
Thanks, Mom.

50
00:04:04,993 --> 00:04:07,171
I'll talk to him.

51
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:08,451
Is he still in his office?

52
00:04:08,451 --> 00:04:10,149
I think so.

53
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:16,105
Thanks, Mom.

54
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:22,060
Robbie! Good luck! Robbie

55
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:40,428
Here are the X-rays you wanted, Dr. Stewart.

56
00:04:40,428 --> 00:04:52,340
Oh. Thank you, Molly.

57
00:04:52,340 --> 00:04:56,218
Now, let me check them.

58
00:04:56,218 --> 00:04:57,796
What do you think?

59
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:03,752
I don't see any breaks or fractures.

60
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:21,620
Well, well. Thank you, Molly.

61
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,620
Thank you.

62
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:23,620
Come in!

63
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:24,420
Hi, Son.

64
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,098
Hi, Dad. Am I interrupting you?

65
00:05:26,098 --> 00:05:28,076
No, no, no, no.

66
00:05:28,076 --> 00:05:28,909
What's up?

67
00:05:28,909 --> 00:05:30,554
Can we talk?

68
00:05:30,554 --> 00:05:31,194
Sure.

69
00:05:31,194 --> 00:05:34,032
I need some help.

70
00:05:34,032 --> 00:05:36,793
Well, that's what fathers are for.

71
00:05:36,793 --> 00:05:38,497
Well, before I go to college,

72
00:05:38,497 --> 00:05:40,967
I have the whole summer ...

73
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:41,707
Yes ...

74
00:05:41,707 --> 00:05:45,981
And I'm planning to get a job for the summer.

75
00:05:45,981 --> 00:05:47,327
And what sort of job?

76
00:05:47,327 --> 00:05:53,039
I applied for a job as a lifeguard at the community pool.

77
00:05:53,039 --> 00:05:55,499
Sounds pretty good.

78
00:05:55,499 --> 00:05:58,832
Yes. I'll be earning pretty good money if I get it.

79
00:05:58,832 --> 00:06:01,619
But right now, I'm kind of short of cash.

80
00:06:01,619 --> 00:06:02,476
Who isn't?

81
00:06:02,476 --> 00:06:05,061
And my friend Alexandra is going back to Greece ...

82
00:06:05,061 --> 00:06:06,700
Nice girl.

83
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,346
We'll all miss her.

84
00:06:08,346 --> 00:06:11,722
Mom says we can give her a going-away surprise party.

85
00:06:11,722 --> 00:06:12,245
Good idea.

86
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:15,556
And I'd like to get her a nice gift ...

87
00:06:15,556 --> 00:06:19,701
What'd you have in mind?

88
00:06:19,701 --> 00:06:22,739
Well, a wristwatch,

89
00:06:22,739 --> 00:06:26,090
so she'll think of me when she looks at the time.

90
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:28,386
Nothing flashy or expensive.

91
00:06:28,386 --> 00:06:31,265
Something simple--but a good one.

92
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:33,091
Sounds fine, Robbie.

93
00:06:33,091 --> 00:06:36,069
Well, I saw a nice watch.

94
00:06:36,069 --> 00:06:37,433
But I'll need a loan.

95
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:39,272
If you could lend me the money,

96
00:06:39,272 --> 00:06:42,025
I could pay you back out of my lifeguard salary.

97
00:06:42,025 --> 00:06:49,480
Well, I guess your mother and I can manage it.

98
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,371
When do you need the money?

99
00:06:52,371 --> 00:06:53,936
Would tomorrow be OK?

100
00:06:53,936 --> 00:06:56,914
You've got it.

101
00:06:56,914 --> 00:06:59,892
Thanks, Dad.

102
00:06:59,892 --> 00:07:02,870
My pleasure, Son.

103
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:05,848
Oh, and, Robbie ...

104
00:07:05,848 --> 00:07:06,181
Yes?

105
00:07:06,181 --> 00:07:08,181
You'll probably want the family car

106
00:07:08,181 --> 00:07:11,804
so you can drive her home after the party.

107
00:07:11,804 --> 00:07:17,760
Could I?

108
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:20,738
If you drive carefully.

109
00:07:20,738 --> 00:07:22,405
I will. Thanks, Dad.

110
00:07:22,405 --> 00:07:23,716
My pleasure.

111
00:07:23,716 --> 00:07:26,694
You're OK, Dad.

112
00:07:26,694 --> 00:07:29,694
You're not so bad yourself, Son.
